/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq -|e2e4","mine":false,"comments":["White starts with 1.e4 and invites a direct fight for the centre. We answer with the Caro-Kann, where an exchange on d5 gives our pieces different plans from an advance to e5."],"shapes":[],"ply":1},{"san":"c6","uci":"c7c6","fenBefore":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1","fenAfter":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","key":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq -|c7c6","mine":true,"comments":["We prepare ...d5 with a pawn that can recapture on that square. The c8 bishop still has an open route outside our pawn chain, which distinguishes this structure from an immediate ...e6 setup."],"shapes":[],"ply":2},{"san":"d4","uci":"d2d4","fenBefore":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","fenAfter":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 2","key":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq -|d2d4","mine":false,"comments":["White places a second pawn in the centre and supports e5."],"shapes":[],"ply":3},{"san":"d5","uci":"d7d5","fenBefore":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 2","fenAfter":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3p4/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 3","key":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq -|d7d5","mine":true,"comments":["We challenge e4 directly and occupy d5 under the protection of c6. White must now choose whether to exchange, advance, or defend the central pawn; each decision produces a different plan for our pieces."],"shapes":[],"ply":4},{"san":"exd5","uci":"e4d5","fenBefore":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3p4/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 3","fenAfter":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3P4/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 3","key":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3p4/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq -|e4d5","mine":false,"comments":["White exchanges the e-pawn and leaves a central pawn on d4. The resulting e-file makes development and control of the central squares more important than an immediate attack."],"shapes":[],"ply":5},{"san":"cxd5","uci":"c6d5","fenBefore":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3P4/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 3","fenAfter":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/8/3p4/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 4","key":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3P4/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq -|c6d5","mine":true,"comments":["We recapture with the c-pawn, keeping a pawn in the centre rather than exposing our queen. Our c-file is now half-open for a rook, while the c8 bishop remains free to develop before ...e6."],"shapes":[],"ply":6},{"san":"Bd3","uci":"f1d3","fenBefore":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/8/3p4/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 4","fenAfter":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/8/3p4/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 1 4","key":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/8/3p4/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq -|f1d3","mine":false,"comments":["White points the bishop toward h7 while keeping both knights flexible. The move order makes c3 and Bf4 natural follow-ups, so our development must account for an early queen attack on b7."],"shapes":[],"ply":7},{"san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fenBefore":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/8/3p4/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 1 4","fenAfter":"r1bqkbnr/pp2pppp/2n5/3p4/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 2 5","key":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/8/3p4/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq -|b8c6","mine":true,"comments":["The queenside knight develops to c6 and immediately increases the pressure against d4. This asks White to support the centre and gives us a useful piece before committing the c8 bishop or deciding how the kingside knight should develop."],"shapes":[],"ply":8},{"san":"c3","uci":"c2c3","fenBefore":"r1bqkbnr/pp2pppp/2n5/3p4/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 2 5","fenAfter":"r1bqkbnr/pp2pppp/2n5/3p4/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 0 5","key":"r1bqkbnr/pp2pppp/2n5/3p4/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq -|c2c3","mine":false,"comments":["White reinforces d4 and gives the queen a route toward b3."],"shapes":[],"ply":9},{"san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fenBefore":"r1bqkbnr/pp2pppp/2n5/3p4/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 0 5","fenAfter":"r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/3p4/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 1 6","key":"r1bqkbnr/pp2pppp/2n5/3p4/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq -|g8f6","mine":true,"comments":["We bring the second knight toward the centre and prepare kingside development. The knight helps control e4, while leaving the c8 bishop free to emerge before our e-pawn fixes the central structure."],"shapes":[],"ply":10},{"san":"Bf4","uci":"c1f4","fenBefore":"r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/3p4/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 1 6","fenAfter":"r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/3p4/3P1B2/2PB4/PP3PPP/RN1QK1NR b KQkq - 2 6","key":"r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/3p4/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq -|c1f4","mine":false,"comments":["White develops actively and eyes c7 along the diagonal from f4. The queen can join on b3, creating pressure against both b7 and d5 before White commits the knights."],"shapes":[],"ply":11},{"san":"Bg4","uci":"c8g4","fenBefore":"r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/3p4/3P1B2/2PB4/PP3PPP/RN1QK1NR b KQkq - 2 6","fenAfter":"r2qkb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/3p4/3P1Bb1/2PB4/PP3PPP/RN1QK1NR w KQkq - 3 7","key":"r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/3p4/3P1B2/2PB4/PP3PPP/RN1QK1NR b KQkq -|c8g4","mine":true,"comments":["We place the bishop outside the pawn chain before playing ...e6. From g4 it watches the route through f3 toward White’s queen, so a later knight development can create useful pressure along that diagonal."],"shapes":[],"ply":12},{"san":"Qb3","uci":"d1b3","fenBefore":"r2qkb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/3p4/3P1Bb1/2PB4/PP3PPP/RN1QK1NR w KQkq - 3 7","fenAfter":"r2qkb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/3p4/3P1Bb1/1QPB4/PP3PPP/RN2K1NR b KQkq - 4 7","key":"r2qkb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/3p4/3P1Bb1/2PB4/PP3PPP/RN1QK1NR w KQkq -|d1b3","mine":false,"comments":["White attacks b7 and d5 at once, hoping our development has left the queenside loose. We answer actively against the queen rather than rush into a passive defence."],"shapes":[],"ply":13},{"san":"Na5","uci":"c6a5","fenBefore":"r2qkb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/3p4/3P1Bb1/1QPB4/PP3PPP/RN2K1NR b KQkq - 4 7","fenAfter"